{"rationale":"All ten use the rule directly: enumerate every subset of removable `o` leaves (at most 7 in the supplied inputs), then test reachability among the unremoved leaves by same-row/same-column jumps. The least subset that disconnects S from T is the uniquely required output; if none does, it is -1. This covers direct S/T alignment, zero/one/multiple cuts, isolated leaves, and dense alternatives without trusting implementation details. 1. test_direct_alignment | requirement: minimum removals or -1 | technique: direct small-input oracle | oracle: output differs from exhaustive minimum | validity: all supplied inputs have <=7 removable leaves. 2. test_one_leaf_cut | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 3. test_alternate_rows | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 4. test_alternate_columns | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 5. test_sparse_disconnect | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 6. test_sparse_offset | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 7. test_single_bridge | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 8. test_remote_leaves | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 9. test_two_cuts | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. 10. test_dense_paths | requirement: same | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact mismatch | validity: exhaustive definition. These are intentionally redundant sharp checks; I would drop test_sparse_offset first.","tests":[{"name":"test_direct_alignment","source":"def test_direct_alignment(run, x):
    p=x.split(); h,w=map(int,p[:2]); g=p[2:]
    s=t=None; o=[]
    for r in range(h):
        for c,ch in enumerate(g[r]):
            if ch=='S': s=(r,c)
            elif ch=='T': t=(r,c)
            elif ch=='o': o.append((r,c))
    best=10**9
