{"rationale":"Each test uses an exhaustive definition-level oracle: choose every root of length at least five, enumerate all following 2/3-letter block partitions, reject equal adjacent blocks, and collect every block in a completed construction. The asserted token sequence enforces the required count and lexicographic order while accepting harmless whitespace variation. 1. test_min_root | requirement: root has >4 letters | technique: boundary/direct oracle | oracle: exact valid suffix list | validity: exhaustive. 2. test_two_tail | requirement: 2-letter suffix allowed | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 3. test_three_tail | requirement: 3-letter suffix allowed | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 4. test_mixed_tail | requirement: appended blocks may have either length | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 5. test_root_choices | requirement: any root longer than four may be chosen | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 6. test_distinct_blocks | requirement: only consecutive equal blocks forbidden | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 7. test_repeated_pattern | requirement: adjacent-block restriction | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 8. test_longer_tail | requirement: all possible suffixes printed | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 9. test_uniform_word | requirement: equality rule applies to strings | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. 10. test_alternating | requirement: distinct strings/order | technique: direct oracle | oracle: exact list | validity: exhaustive. I would drop test_alternating first because all use the same complete oracle.","tests":[{"name":"test_min_root","source":"def test_min_root(run, x):
    s = x.strip()
    n = len(s)
    want = set()
    def dfs(i, prev, path):
        if i == n:
            want.update(path)
            return
        for z in (2, 3):
            if i + z <= n:
                block = s[i:i+z]
                if block != prev:
                    dfs(i+z, block, path+[block])
    for root in range(5, n+1):
        dfs(root, None, [])
    tokens = run(x).split()
    assert tokens == [str(len(want))] + sorted(want)"},{"name":"test_two_tail","source":"def test_two_tail(run, x):
    s = x.strip()
    n = len(s)
    want = set()
    def dfs(i, previous, used):
        if i == n:
            want.update(used)
            return
        for length in (2, 3):
            if i + length <= n:
                part = s[i:i+length]
                if part != previous:
                    dfs(i + length, part, used + [part])
    for root_length in range(5, n + 1):
        dfs(root_length, None, [])
    got = run(x).split()
    assert got == [str(len(want))] + sorted(want)"},{"name":"test_three_tail","source":"def test_three_tail(run, x):
    s = x.strip()
