{"rationale":"1. test_matching_bfs | requirement: output the maximum sum over all divisions into pairs | technique: direct small-input oracle | oracle: enumerate every pairing using tree distances | validity: all supplied trees have n=8.
2. test_mask_dp | requirement: same maximum | technique: decision-rule DP over unmatched universities | oracle: exact maximum matching recurrence | validity: recurrence considers every legal pair partition.
3. test_edge_contributions | requirement: maximize pairwise path lengths | technique: tree-edge cut oracle | oracle: each edge contributes min(s,2k-s) | validity: this is attainable for tree terminal pairings.
4. test_pairing_recursive | requirement: each university occurs once | technique: exhaustive enumeration | oracle: pair first remaining terminal with every other | validity: uniquely covers all pairings.
5. test_distance_matching | requirement: roads have unit length | technique: direct oracle | oracle: BFS distances plus exhaustive pairing | validity: BFS gives tree path lengths.
6. test_subset_optimum | requirement: maximum total distance | technique: bitmask direct oracle | oracle: optimal-substructure recurrence | validity: every partition selects a partner for its first bit.
7. test_cut_sum | requirement: total cable path length | technique: edge-cut exact oracle | oracle: sum forced crossing capacities | validity: correct for every supplied tree.
8. test_all_pairings | requirement: legal pair division maximizes sum | technique: exhaustive direct oracle | oracle: enumerate legal divisions | validity: n=8 makes it small.
9. test_terminal_dp | requirement: every university used once | technique: subset DP | oracle: exact disjoint-pair maximum | validity: mask removes both paired terminals.
10. test_unit_tree_oracle | requirement: all roads length one | technique: direct oracle | oracle: BFS and exhaustive pairing | validity: computes stated distances. I would drop the duplicated recursive oracle first.","tests":[{"name":"test_matching_bfs","source":"def test_matching_bfs(run, x):
    a=list(map(int,x.split())); n,k=a[:2]; u=[v-1 for v in a[2:2+2*k]]; p=2+2*k; g=[[] for _ in range(n)]
    for i in range(p,len(a),2):
        v,w=a[i]-1,a[i+1]-1; g[v].append(w); g[w].append(v)
    d=[]
    for s in u:
        q=[s]; z=[-1]*n; z[s]=0
        for v in q:
            for w in g[v]:
                if z[w]<0: z[w]=z[v]+1; q.append(w)
        d.append(z)
    def f(t):
        if not t:return 0
        return max(d[t[0]][t[i]]+f(t[1:i]+t[i+1:]) for i in range(1,len(t)))
    out=run(x)
    assert int(out.strip())==f(u)"},{"name":"test_mask_dp","source":"def test_mask_dp(run, x):
    a=list(map(int,x.split())); n,k=a[:2]; u=[v-1 for v in a[2:2+2*k]; p=2+2*k; g=[[] for _ in range(n)]
    for i in range(p,len(a),2):
        v,w=a[i]-1,a[i+1]-1; g[v]+=[w]; g[w]+=[v]
    D=[]
    for s in u:
        q=[s]; z=[-1]*n; z[s]=0
        for v in q:
            for w in g[v]:
                if z[w]==-1:z[w]=z[v]+1;q.append(w)
        D.append([z[t] for t in u])
    m={0:0}
    def f(mask):
        if mask in m:return m[mask]
        i=(mask&-mask).bit_length()-1; m[mask]=max(D[i][j]+f(mask^(1<<i)^(1<<j)) for j in range(i+1,len(u)) if mask>>j&1); return m[mask]
    out=run(x)
    assert int(out.strip())==f((1<<len(u))-1)"},{"name":"test_edge_contributions","source":"def test_edge_contributions(run, x):
    a=list(map(int,x.split())); n,k=a[:2]; mark=set(v-1 for v in a[2:2+2*k]); p=2+2*k; g=[[] for _ in range(n)]
    for i in range(p,len(a),2):
        v,w=a[i]-1,a[i+1]-1; g[v].append(w);g[w].append(v)
    par=[-1]*n; order=[0]; par[0]=0
    for v in order:
        for w in g[v]:
            if par[w]<0: par[w]=v;order.append(w)
    c=[int(i in mark) for i in range(n)]; ans=0
    for v in order[:0:-1]:
        ans+=min(c[v],2*k-c[v]); c[par[v]]+=c[v]
    out=run(x)
    assert int(out.strip())==ans"},{"name":"test_pairing_recursive","source":"def test_pairing_recursive(run, x):
    a=list(map(int,x.split())); n,k=a[:2]; u=[v-1 for v in a[2:2+2*k]]; g=[[] for _ in range(n)]; p=2+2*k
    for i in range(p,len(a),2):
        v,w=a[i]-1,a[i+1]-1;g[v].append(w);g[w].append(v)
    def dist(s):
        q=[s]; r={s:0}
        for v in q:
            for w in g[v]:
                if w not in r:r[w]=r[v]+1;q.append(w)
        return r
    ds=[dist(v) for v in u]
    def opt(v):
        return 0 if not v else max(ds[v[0]][v[i]]+opt(v[1:i]+v[i+1:]) for i in range(1,len(v)))
